A||N||6||DaveL||Shifty Automatic||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||02-18-2000||08:51 AM||||A simple? question about an auto tranny 87 2.5 DIS. This transmission usually shifts normally. By that I mean without a lot of throttle, it shifts from first into second and third by around 30 mph. But every now and then, it doesnt want to shift from first to second untill around 3500 rpm regardless of pedal pressure. Same from second to third. Then, without warning, it works normally again.This means I sometimes end up going around 55 mph to get it into third. Maybe someone put a shift kit in it, I don't know. It downshifts normally with moderate gas pedal pressure. This is causing me to get bad mileage from cruising around in second in areas where I cant go fast enough to hit third when its in this mood. Are the shift points controlled totally by the ECM ? I remember when there were vacuum modulaters that did this.  Old school I guess. I had the tranny flushed at Grease Monkey, but didn't change the filter. Can a clogged filter cause high shift points?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||02-18-2000||09:09 AM||||You have a 4 pin connector on the forward side of the transmission.  Thats the Torque Converter Clutch Lockup Solenoid.  Unplug that connector and test drive the car.  If that fixes your problem, you need to replace the lockup solenoid.  Do not leave the connector unplugged for a long period of time if that seems to solve your problem.  In the long term, unplugging the connector can shorten the life of the tranny.<P>Do a search for "TCC" and/or "lockup solenoid" as weve discussed this stuff before. I havent had to deal with this yet on my auto, but it seems like I read here that replacing the solenoid wasnt a huge job.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-18-2000||09:23 AM||||Sometimes a sticky valve in the valve-body will cause what you're describing. It has to build up more pressure in order to shift.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-18-2000||09:57 AM||||Shifting is not controlled by the ECM. The TC lockup is the only control the ECM has.<P>This doesn't sound like a TC problem. Try running a cleaner thru. dirt in the valve body will sometimes clear that way. I'll assume that you checked the fluid level.<P>A clogged filter would affect the thing nearly constantly. There is so much surface area on the filter tho that it has to be pretty badly flooded with crud to plug.<P>A TV cable that's out of adjustment or bad will also mess up shifting.||||reg||1
Z||000004||burdell1||02-18-2000||12:28 PM||||My guess would be the "TV" or "kickdown" cable....check to see if any of the wires at the end of it are frayed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||burdell1||02-18-2000||12:29 PM||||how much is a new lockup solenoid usually?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||02-18-2000||04:24 PM||||not very expencive. 20$us or less last I heard. might even have them on wrenchead.com or carparts.com. If not then you'll have to get it from a GM/Pontiac dealer. I haven't looked.||||reg||1
